# Cuebert — UE C++ coding standards

Applies when editing Unreal C++ translation units and module build scripts. Pair with `.cursor/rules/cuebert-engineering.mdc` for the Structured Reasoning Gate and Build Verification Gate.

## Reflection macros

- Use **`UCLASS`**, **`USTRUCT`**, **`UPROPERTY`**, **`UFUNCTION`** with explicit specifiers (`EditAnywhere`, `BlueprintReadOnly`, `Replicated`, etc.)—avoid default-reflecting everything.
- Every reflected class/struct body includes **`GENERATED_BODY()`** in the type declaration per UE5 code generation rules for that type.
- Match `meta` tags to editor and network needs; do not duplicate tags inconsistently across header/impl.

## Naming (Epic style)

- **`F`** — plain structs, value types.
- **`U`** — `UObject` derivatives (components, non-actor objects).
- **`A`** — `AActor` derivatives.
- **`E`** — `UENUM` / enum classes exposed to reflection where applicable.
- Keep project-wide prefixes consistent with existing modules.

## Garbage collection & ownership

- Any stored **`UObject*`** that must survive or be reachable from GC must be visible to the collector—typically **`UPROPERTY()`** on member fields.
- Do **not** use raw C++ **`new`** for `UObject` / `AActor` construction; use `NewObject`, spawn helpers, or subsystem patterns per module conventions.
- Use **`TWeakObjectPtr`**, soft object paths, or other non-owning handles for back-links and caches to avoid accidental cycles and stale strong refs.
- Clean up **`FTimerHandle`**, delegates, and bound callbacks when owning actors/components tear down.

## Logging

- Use **`UE_LOG(Category, Verbosity, TEXT("Format"), ...)`** with a module- or feature-stable category; avoid ad-hoc `printf` / `std::cout` in game code paths.
- Do not log secrets, tokens, or full user payloads.

## Scope guardrails

- **`DECLARED_SCOPE`** and harness inputs are authoritative per `docs/_ai_system/agents/agent-play-author.md` §2–§4: do not edit paths outside the declared game roots.
- **Surfaces** for Unreal C++ disk work: `Source/**/*.cpp`, `Source/**/*.h`, `Plugins/**` as allowed by scope; see **§5.1** of the same doc.
- Do **not** modify **`Engine/`**, **`Intermediate/`**, **`Binaries/`**, or generated trees unless explicitly allow-listed (normally never).
- Engine **`Config/*.ini`** and similar require explicit allow-list entries in scope (`ENGINE_CONFIG_ALLOWLIST` / expanded `DECLARED_SCOPE`); otherwise refuse.
- Align Remote Control / harness mutations with `docs/_ai_system/standards/unreal-bridge-contract.md` when editor automation is involved.

## Module dependencies & includes

- Declare all link dependencies in **`*.Build.cs`** (`PublicDependencyModuleNames`, `PrivateDependencyModuleNames`, `DynamicallyLoadedModuleNames` as needed).
- Prefer **include-what-you-use**: minimal headers in `.h`, move heavy includes to `.cpp`; use forward declarations where possible.
- After changing `*.Build.cs`, expect UBT to rebuild affected targets—record evidence per `docs/_ai_system/standards/build-verify-gaming.md` when handing off.

## Quick macro & specifier reminders

| Macro | Typical use |
|-------|-------------|
| `UCLASS()` | UObject types exposed to editor / reflection |
| `USTRUCT()` | Plain data bags that may replicate or serialize |
| `UPROPERTY()` | Editor visibility, replication, GC roots, config |
| `UFUNCTION()` | BlueprintCallable, RPCs, delegates |

Prefer minimal specifiers: add `BlueprintReadOnly` / `Replicated` only when the feature needs them.

